s continuing to weigh on prices and realisations. Exports from the US to Southeast Asia were particularly impacted by unremunerative pricing. In this environment, our immediate priorities remain operational excellence, structural cost reduction, cash generation and disciplined capital allocation. Despite a resilient standalone operating performance, our consolidated results were impacted by a sharp rise in UK natural gas costs. The prolonged Middle East conflict continued to drive inflation in key inputs, including limestone and CO₂, as well as energy, freight, and logistics costs across our operations. Additionally, the temporary suspension of Kenya operations weighed on consolidated performance. We continue to advance our LIFE strategy, progressively shaping the portfolio towards sustainability-led, application-focused and less cyclical businesses, while strengthening the competitiveness of our core operations. In Living Essentials, the demand outlook remains positive, supported by premiumisation and increasing consumption across food, feed, pharmaceutical and beverage applications. Salt and bicarbonates are expected to provide stable growth, while prebiotics offer attractive long-term opportunities driven by increasing consumer focus on health and wellness. In Industrial Essentials, particularly soda ash, the near to medium term outlook remains challenging due to excess global capacity, weak pricing and geopolitical and cost pressures. We will remain focused on improving efficiency, optimising our glo"
