      "pdf_extracted_text": "Ref: SGL/Compliance/2026-27/108 November 07, 2026 Listing / Compliance Department Listing/Compliance Department BSE Limited National Stock Exchange of India Limited Floor 25, P J Towers, Exchange Plaza, Dalal Street, Bandra Kurla Complex, Mumbai – 400 001 Bandra (East), Mumbai – 400 051 Scrip Code: 532993 Symbol: SEJALLTD Subject: Press Release ‘Sejal Glass Limited Proposes Rs. 40.80 Crore Acquisition of Architectural And Automotive Glass Business’ Reference: Intimation under Regulation 30 of the SEBI (Listing Obligations and Disclosure Requirements), Regulations, 2015. Dear Sir/Madam, In accordance with Regulation 30 of the SEBI Listing Regulations, please ϐind enclosed herewith a copy of the press release being issued by the Company, titled “Sejal Glass Limited Proposes Rs. 40.80 Crore Acquisition of Architectural and Automotive Glass Business”. This is for your information and records. Thanking you, Yours faithfully, For Sejal Glass Limited Ashwin S. Shetty Vice President – Operations & Company Secretary – Compliance Ofϐicer Membership No.: A20942 Encl.: as above Sejal Glass Limited Proposes ₹40.80 Cr Acquisition Of Architectural And Automotive Glass Business; Strengthens Its Manufacturing Presence In South India Proposed acquisition of Magnumtuff India Private Limited's business undertaking is expected to expand the Company's manufacturing network to four facilities in India and strengthen its presence across key regional markets. Mumbai, 7th November, 2026 – Sejal Glass Limited (Sejal Glass, The Company), (NSE Code: SEJALLTD/ BSE Code: 532993), a manufacturer of high-quality architectural glass solutions, has announced that its Board of Directors has approved the proposed execution of a Business Transfer Agreement (BTA) with Magnumtuff India Private Limited for the acquisition of its Architectural Glass and Automotive Glass business undertaking on a going-concern basis through a slump sale. The proposed acquisition, together with the purchase of the associated factory land and building, involves an aggregate lump-sum consideration of ₹40.80 crore. The identified business undertaking, which includes manufacturing facilities, business assets, inventory, intellectual property, technical know-how, customer and vendor relationships, contracts and employees, reported operating revenue of ₹36.20 crore during FY26. Key Highlights of the Proposed Acquisition • ₹40.80 Cr Acquisition Consideration – Proposed acquisition of the identified Architectural Glass and Automotive Glass business undertaking, along with the associated immovable property. • Expansion to Four Manufacturing Facilities in India – The proposed acquisition is expected to establish an additional manufacturing facility in South India, expanding the Company's manufacturing footprint to four facilities in India. • Strategic Karnataka Location – The facility is situated at Nainglaj Village, Chikodi Taluka, Belgaum District, Karnataka, providing access to markets across Karnataka, Maharashtra, Goa and adjoining regions. • ₹36.20 Cr Operating Revenue – The identified business undertaking recorded operating revenue of ₹36.20 crore during FY26. • Broader Product and Business Capabilities – The acquisition will add established Architectural Glass and Automotive Glass operations to the Company's existing business portfolio. Strengthening Regional Reach and Operational Capabilities The proposed acquisition marks an important step in Sejal Glass Limited's plans to expand its manufacturin"
