      "pdf_extracted_text": "November 7, 2026 To, To, BSE Limited National Stock Exchange of India Limited PhirozeJeejeebhoy Towers, Exchange Plaza, Dalal Street, Bandra Kurla Complex, Mumbai- 400 001. Mumbai- 400 051. Scrip Code: 526729 Scrip Code: GOLDIAM EQ Dear Sir/Madam, Sub: Press Release in respect of Unaudited Financial Results for the quarter and half year ended September 30, 2026 Enclosed herewith please find the Revised Press Release on the Performance of the Company for the quarter and half year ended September 30, 2026. The aforesaid Press Release will also be uploaded on the website of the Company i.e. www.goldiam.com Kindly take the above on record and oblige. Thanking you, Yours faithfully, For Goldiam International Limited Pankaj Parkhiya Company Secretary & Compliance Officer Registered Office Gems & Jewellery Complex, Santacruz Electronics Export Processing Zone, Andheri (East), Mumbai‐400096. India Phones: (022) 28291893/28290396/28292397 Fax : (022) 28292885 Email:‐ investorrelations@goldiam.com Website: www.goldiam.com PRESS RELEASE Goldiam International’s consolidated Q2FY27 PAT jumps 58% YoY to ₹ 494 mn. Consolidated Revenue for Q2 FY2027 at ₹ 2916.6 million - up 44% Y-o-Y. Closes highest-ever Q2 and H1 Report on Revenue & PAT. Consolidated H1 revenue and PAT up by 50% and 90% respectively The board declares an interim dividend of 100% i.e. ₹ 2 per share Mumbai, November 07, 2026: Goldiam International Ltd. (Goldiam), an integrated manufacturer and supplier of fine diamond jewellery to leading retailers and wholesalers in the USA, has announced its results for the second quarter and the half year ended on September 30, 2026. Q2 & H1 FY 2027 key highlights (Consolidated) Goldiam’s total revenue, which predominantly comes from B2B diamond jewellery exports, continued its growth momentum in Q2 of FY 2027 backed by a sustained demand from large global retailers. Goldiam reported a total revenue of ₹ 2916.6 million for Q2 FY 2027, up by 44%. Total revenue for H1 at ₹ 6553.2 million, grew sharply by 50%. Goldiam reported an EBITDA of ₹ 736 million for Q2 FY2027 which was up by 55.3%. EBITDA margin for Q2 FY27 stood at 25.24%, up 176 basis points over Q2 of FY26. H1 FY27 EBITDA at ₹ 1775.3 million grew by a 87.8%, with EBITDA margin of 27.1%, up by 550 basis points over H1FY26. Profit after Tax for Q2 FY2027 at ₹ 494 million grew by 58% Y-o-Y; whereas PAT for H1 FY2027 at ₹ 1233.7 million grew by 90%. The Board of Directors has declared 1st interim dividend @ ₹ 2/- (100%) per equity share of ₹ 2/- each, amounting to ₹ 301.11 million. Lab Grown Diamond jewellery exports contributed 91.2% to the overall export sales mix during Q2 FY27, compared to 90% in Q2 FY26. Online revenue accounted for 19.4% of the revenue during Q2 FY27. Goldiam’s order book position as on September 30, 2026 was at about ₹ 2250 million. Cash and Cash Equivalents (including investments) were at ₹ 4578.25 million as at September 30, 2026. Financial Highlights (Consolidated) – Q2 & H1 FY2027 Particulars (₹ Mn) Q2FY27 Q2FY26 YoY H1FY27 H1FY26 YoY Revenue 2917 2019 44% 6,553.2 4,376.0 49.8% EBITDA 736 474 55.3% 1775.3 945.4 87.8% EBITDA margin 25.24% 23.48% 176 bps 27.1% 21.6% 550 bps PAT 494 314 58% 1233.7 649.7 89.9% PAT margin 16.94% 15.53% 141 bps 18.8% 14.8% 398 bps EPS (Diluted) 2.96* 2.85 3.9% 9.5 6.00 58.5% *adjusted post bonus shares issue ORIGEM update As on date, Goldiam has 29 operational ORIGEM stores selling lab grown diamond jewellery across key cities. For Q2 FY2027"
