      "pdf_extracted_text": "PPAP Automotive Limited GSTIN: 07AAACP5144P3Z1 & 07AAACP5144P2Z2 7th November, 2026 The Listing Department The Listing Department BSE Limited The National Stock Exchange of India Limited Phiroze Jeejeebhoy Towers, Exchange Plaza, Dalal Street, Bandra Kurla Complex, Mumbai – 400001 Bandra (E), Mumbai - 400051 Symbol: 532934 Symbol: PPAP Subject: Media release on the financial results for the quarter & half year ended 30th September, 2026. Dear Sir Pursuant to Regulation 30 of the Securities and Exchange Board of India (Listing Obligations and Disclosure Requirements) Regulations, 2015, please find enclosed the media release on the financial results of the Company for the quarter & half year ended 30th September, 2026. This is for your information and record. Thanking you, Yours faithfully, For PPAP Automotive Limited Pankhuri Agarwal Company Secretary & Compliance Officer Registered office: 54, Okhla Industrial Estate, Phase III, New Delhi-110020 +91-011-62560000 info@ppapco.com www.ppapco.in CIN: L74899DL1995PLC073281 PPAP Automotive Limited GSTIN: 07AAACP5144P3Z1 & 07AAACP5144P2Z2 Earnings Release PPAP Automotive achieves highest-ever quarterly and half-yearly revenues, with robust order wins of INR 429 crore driven by strong EV traction New Delhi, November 06, 2026: PPAP Automotive Limited, part of the Ajay Group and a leading automotive components manufacturer with a diversified portfolio and solutions, today announced its unaudited financial results for the quarter & half-year ended 30th September 2026. Key Consolidated Financial Highlights for Q2 & H1FY27: • Record Quarterly & Half Yearly Revenue: Revenue from operations grew by 29.8% YoY to INR 177.8 crore in Q2FY27 and 31.8% YoY to INR 334.2 crore in H1FY27, supported by strong execution of order book and broad-based growth across the automobile industry • Strong EBITDA Growth: EBITDA increased by 23.0% YoY to INR 15.7 Crores in Q2FY27 and 27.4% YoY to INR 28.1 Crores in H1FY27. Improving operating efficiencies helped cushion the impact of lower gross margins, with EBITDA margins stood at 8.8% and 8.4%, respectively • Turnaround in Profitability: Consolidated PAT stood at INR 2.5 Crores in Q2FY27, while H1FY27 reported a profit of INR 3.3 Crores, marking a turnaround from a loss of INR 2.3 Crores in H1FY26 Key Standalone Financial Highlights for Q1FY27: • Record Revenue Performance: Achieved highest-ever quarterly and half-yearly standalone revenue of INR 165.1 Crores and INR 309.3 Crores, growing 24.4% and 26.7% YoY, respectively • Consistent EBITDA Growth: EBITDA rose 12.0% YoY to INR 14.9 Crores in Q2FY27 and 16.8% to INR 27.0 Crores in H1FY27 • Significant Improvement in Profitability: PAT increased to INR 3.5 Crores in Q2FY27 from INR 1.9 Crores, while H1FY27 PAT rose to INR 5.8 Crores from INR 1.6 Crores, registering a 269% growth Key Business Highlights – Q2 & H1FY27 Robust Order Wins of INR ~429 Crores in H1FY27, driven by Strong EV Order Momentum: o PPAP secured orders worth approximately INR 298 crore during Q2FY27, taking cumulative order wins for H1FY27 to INR 429 crore. Q2FY27 orders registered a strong sequential growth of 127.6% over Q1FY27 o EV-related order wins increased approximately 5.8 times to ~INR 157 crore in H1FY27, compared to INR 27 Crores in H1FY26. EV programs contributed INR 92 Crores to Q2FY27 order wins, reflecting increasing participation in the electric mobility segment Registere d office: 54, Okhla Industrial Estate, Phase III, New Delhi-110020 "
